reasoning_details.text:
I noticed a CSS typo I accidentally left: 

```css
.plant__detail {
  margin-top: 14px;
  ...
  animation: panel-in .3sease both;
}

.plant__detail { animation-name: panel-in; animation-duration: .3s; animation-timing-function: ease; }
```

`.3sease` is invalid — the shorthand will just be dropped for the invalid part (browsers ignore invalid values in shorthand, could drop the whole declaration). Then I re-declare with the individual properties, which fixes it. Still, let me clean it up to avoid confusion.

